r a cumulative widening where a module that was described as having N operations now has noticeably more. Temporary shims and internal helpers do not count. For small missions (under 5 feature tasks) a one-line \"no drift observed\" note in the handoff is sufficient -- this step exists to catch cumulative drift across many tasks, which rarely occurs in short missions. This catches drift that per-task scrutiny cannot see.\n+3. **Module shape re-check (mandatory for missions with 5+ feature tasks; optional otherwise).** Re-read design.md's module descriptions. For each module, compare the description to what the code actually exposes -- in whatever form is natural for the project (public functions, React props, HTTP endpoints, CLI flags, exported types, data schemas, message topics, job parameters, config keys, whatever contract callers actually depend on). Verify that every domain type in the Type Catalog exists in the committed code with a matching name. If reality has drifted meaningfully from the description, either update design.md to match (deliberate change) or refactor the code back (unintended drift). If Type Catalog names have drifted, resolve them by either updating design.md to match the code (deliberate change) or refactoring the code to match design.md (unintended drift). \"Meaningful drift\" means: any public surface item added, removed, or renamed that is not reflected in design.md; any change to the vocabulary or contract callers depend on; or a cumulative widening where a module that was described as having N operations now has noticeably more. Temporary shims and internal helpers do not count. For small missions (under 5 feature tasks) a one-line \"no drift observed\" note in the handoff is sufficient -- this step exists to catch cumulative drift across many tasks, which rarely occurs in short missions. This catches drift that per-task scrutiny cannot see.\n \n    Write the findings to `mission/validations/module-shape-audit.md` -- a short free-form note listing each module, whether drift was found, and what was done about it (\"no drift,\" \"design.md updated,\" or \"refactored\"). No required format; the file exists as a record that the check happened.\n \ndiff --git a/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md b/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\nindex 5d45cdf..b81bddd 100644\n--- a/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\n+++ b/skills/mission/templates/design-template.md\n@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@ List each planned module or major component. Use this table format:\n ## Type Catalog\n \n List domain types only. Type names must come from `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` when the term exists there. Do not include field-level detail.\n+Domain types model the problem space; exclude technical helpers such as CLI parsers, test fixtures, and generic containers unless they are public compatibility surfaces.\n \n | Type name | Purpose | Owning module |\n |-----------|---------|---------------|\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
