4.3 when generating design.md. The Type Catalog section starts at the line \"## Type Catalog\".\n    17\t- `skills/mission/SKILL.md` is the main mission skill file. The module shape re-check is item 3 under \"Mandatory Closing Tasks\" in Phase 8.\n    18\t\n    19\t## Key Terms (from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md)\n    20\t- **Type Catalog**: A design.md section listing domain types with name, purpose, and owning module. Type names are drawn from the glossary when a matching term exists; types not in the glossary are named by the worker.\n    21\t- **Domain type**: A type that models the problem space. Excludes technical helpers unless they are public compatibility surfaces.\n    22\t- **Module shape re-check**: A mandatory closing task that compares design.md module descriptions to actual code surface area.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Domain Types\n    25\tNone for this task. This mission modifies markdown templates only and introduces no domain types.\n    26\t\n    27\t## What Previous Tasks Built\n    28\t### Task 1: Add Domain Types section to worker brief template\n    29\t- Modified: skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md (+10 lines)\n    30\t- Added section: \"## Domain Types\" at line 15, after \"## Key Terms\", before \"## What Previous Tasks Built\"\n    31\t- Section includes: exact-name instruction, Type Catalog placeholder (Produces/Consumes), \"None for this task\" fallback\n    32\t\n    33\t## Downstream Consumers\n    34\tTask 3 (README) references these changes but does not consume them programmatically.\n    35\t\n    36\t## Procedures\n    37\t- Edit `skills/mission/templates/design-template.md` and `skills/mission/SKILL.md`\n    38\t- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-2] Add domain type boundary and Type Catalog name verification\"\n    39\t- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/domain-vocabulary-type-names/mission/handoffs/task-2.md\n    40\t\n    41\t## Handoff Report Format\n    42\t- Task: Task 2 - Add domain type bo