 is the project's primary documentation.\n    18\t\n    19\t## Architecture\n    20\t`README.md` is in the project root. It describes the mission workflow, skills, and architecture. Changes should be woven into the existing narrative, not added as a new section.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Key Terms (from UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md)\n    23\t- **Type Catalog**: A design.md section listing domain types with name, purpose, and owning module.\n    24\t- **Domain type**: A type that models the problem space. Excludes technical helpers unless they are public compatibility surfaces.\n    25\t\n    26\t## Domain Types\n    27\tNone for this task.\n    28\t\n    29\t## What Previous Tasks Built\n    30\t### Task 1: Add Domain Types section to worker brief template\n    31\t- Modified: skills/mission/templates/worker-brief.md (+10 lines)\n    32\t- Added section: \"## Domain Types\" at line 15, after \"## Key Terms\", before \"## What Previous Tasks Built\"\n    33\t- Section includes: exact-name instruction, Type Catalog placeholder (Produces/Consumes), \"None for this task\" fallback\n    34\t\n    35\t### Task 2: Add domain type boundary and Type Catalog name verification\n    36\t- Modified: skills/mission/templates/design-template.md (+1 line)\n    37\t- Modified: skills/mission/SKILL.md (+1 line, -1 line -- extended module shape re-check paragraph)\n    38\t- design-template.md: added domain type boundary sentence after \"List domain types only...\" in Type Catalog section\n    39\t- SKILL.md: added Type Catalog name verification + drift resolution to module shape re-check closing task\n    40\t\n    41\t## Downstream Consumers\n    42\tNone.\n    43\t\n    44\t## Procedures\n    45\t- Edit `README.md` only\n    46\t- Commit all changes in a single commit with message: \"[task-3] Update README to reflect domain vocabulary changes\"\n    47\t- Write your handoff report to openspec/changes/domain-vocabulary-type-names/mission/handoffs/task-3.md\n    48\t\n    49\t## Handoff Report